\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces A computed marked pair in the running example. Left: the cover. Right: a zoom of its marked spokes. Dashed lines are the rays from $w_5$ and $w_6$, in the direction that is vertical in the exact layout. Thick spokes carry the tokens; blue arrows show $D$.}}{8}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The second move on the same object, before and after, in the zoomed region. Both rays are drawn. The token moves to its partner crossing; its cycle reverses when the partner is an $r$-spoke.}}{8}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Drawing-free marks on the same triangulation. Each row is a tree path from its white face to the outer face $f_4$. Squares are bounded black faces; circles are white faces or the outer face. A thick green square is a marked step. Labels give the turned corner and its turn sign; the selected corner equals the turned corner at every marked step. Face IDs follow \texttt  {running.json}.}}{9}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
